Subject: [PATCH] winex11: don't let the window manager own tool-window and
 layered popups

A WS_POPUP that carries WS_SYSMENU is currently handed to the window manager.
Menus, tooltips and drop shadows are not application windows on Windows and are
never WM-managed there; handing them over lets the WM apply its own policies to
them. KDE, for one, moves an off-screen window back onto the screen -- and a
toolkit that positions its own chrome relative to a popup then sees that
geometry change underneath it.

Measured with rekordbox 7.2.18 (JUCE 8) on wine-11.15 + KWin. Its menu popups
carry WS_SYSMENU, and JUCE surrounds every popup with four 14 px drop-shadow
windows. For a menu opening at x = 1 the left shadow lands at x = -13; KWin
moves it to x = 0; JUCE observes the move and dismisses the entire menu 11 ms
after it was mapped:

    File menu   mapped at +0.019 s, hidden at +0.030 s
    View menu   mapped at +0.014 s, hidden at +2.102 s (by the user)

The visible result was that the File menu and the application's view-mode
selector never opened at all while the window was maximised at x = 0, and both
opened perfectly once the window was moved 14 px to the right -- a cliff exactly
at the shadow width:

    window x    File menu opens    left shadow would be at
         0          0/2                  -13
         8          0/2                   -5
        12          0/2                   -1
        14          1/2                   +1
        60          1/2                  +47

A standalone reproducer confirms the rule is WS_SYSMENU and nothing else. Four
windows of the same shape, created at 0,0 and moved into place, then re-read
after settling:

    WS_POPUP, TOOLWINDOW                     -13,36  ->  -13,36   stays
    WS_POPUP, TOOLWINDOW|LAYERED             -13,586 ->  -13,586  stays
    WS_POPUP|WS_SYSMENU, TOOLWINDOW|LAYERED  -13,800 ->    0,800  MOVED
    WS_POPUP|WS_SYSMENU, same but on-screen   32,800 ->   32,800  stays

get_mwm_decorations_for_style() already returns 0 immediately for
WS_EX_TOOLWINDOW and WS_EX_LAYERED, i.e. winex11 already treats these as
undecorated chrome. This makes is_window_managed() agree with it.

With the patch, every popup in the application opens 4/4 with the window
maximised at x = 0, and the off-screen shadow stays where the toolkit put it
(observed at x = -4 in the X tree).

---
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
@@ -451,15 +451,39 @@
     if ((style & WS_CAPTION) == WS_CAPTION) return TRUE;
     /* windows with thick frame are managed */
     if (style & WS_THICKFRAME) return TRUE;
+    ex_style = NtUserGetWindowLongW( hwnd, GWL_EXSTYLE );
     if (style & WS_POPUP)
     {
+        /* RBW-POPUP: menus, tooltips and drop shadows are chrome, not
+         * application windows, and Windows never lets a window manager own
+         * them. Handing them over lets the WM enforce its own policies on
+         * them -- KDE moves an off-screen one back onto the screen -- and a
+         * toolkit that positions its chrome relative to a popup then sees the
+         * geometry change underneath it and tears the popup down.
+         *
+         * Measured with rekordbox 7.2.18 (JUCE 8): its menu popups carry
+         * WS_SYSMENU, so the test below claimed them. Each popup is surrounded
+         * by four 14 px drop-shadow windows; for a menu opening at x = 1 the
+         * left one lands at x = -13, KWin moves it to x = 0, and JUCE dismisses
+         * the whole menu 11 ms after mapping it. The result was that the File
+         * menu and the view-mode selector never opened at all while the window
+         * was maximised at x = 0, and opened perfectly once it was moved 14 px
+         * right.
+         *
+         * get_mwm_decorations_for_style() below already treats both of these
+         * ex-styles as undecorated chrome; this keeps the two consistent. */
+        if (ex_style & (WS_EX_TOOLWINDOW | WS_EX_LAYERED))
+        {
+            TRACE( "RBW-POPUP %p: tool/layered popup, not managed (style %#x ex %#x)\n",
+                   hwnd, (int)style, (int)ex_style );
+            return FALSE;
+        }
         /* popup with sysmenu == caption are managed */
         if (style & WS_SYSMENU) return TRUE;
         /* full-screen popup windows are managed */
         if (fullscreen) return TRUE;
     }
     /* application windows are managed */
-    ex_style = NtUserGetWindowLongW( hwnd, GWL_EXSTYLE );
     if (ex_style & WS_EX_APPWINDOW) return TRUE;
     /* windows that own popups are managed */
     if (has_owned_popups( hwnd )) return TRUE;
